══ 5. what a wider ceiling actually costs, in wei ══
  fee used: 566330400 wei/gas (live estimateFeesPerGas, the same call executor.ts makes)

  THE CEILING IS A REFUSAL THRESHOLD, NOT AN ALLOWANCE. gas-limits.ts:312-331 applies
  headroom to the ESTIMATE and then compares the total to absoluteMax; absoluteMax never
  enters a signed limit. So raising it cannot make any operation cost one wei more —
  it can only stop refusing operations that genuinely estimate between the two numbers.

  ceiling-sized PREFUND (EntryPoint requires the payer to HOLD total x maxFeePerGas):
     3,000,000 gas -> 1,698,991,200,000,000 wei = 0.001698991 ETH
    12,000,000 gas -> 6,795,964,800,000,000 wei = 0.006795965 ETH
    delta          -> 5,096,973,600,000,000 wei = 0.005096974 ETH

  WORST CASE AN ATTACKER CAN ACTUALLY DRAW, per (account, permissionId):
    the widest operation the gate admits is one whose ESTIMATE clears the ceiling.
    measured full-wall renewal: raw 7,530,220, bounded 9,450,410
    signed prefund at that size: 5,352,054,475,464,000 wei = 0.005352054 ETH
    gas actually BURNED is what execution uses, not the limit; the landed 10,964-byte
    enable on 4663 (tx 0x323e8050…) used 5,867,332 = 0.003322848 ETH.

    SELF-PAYING (no sponsor): every wei of that is the ATTACKER'S OWN. The house's
      exposure from widening the ceiling is 0 wei. executor.ts's prefund check
      (held >= bounded.total x feeCeiling) still refuses an account that cannot cover it.
    SPONSORED (cfg.sponsorGasEnabled): the house pays. Exposure per admitted enable is
      the gas USED, ~5,867,332 -> 0.003322848 ETH, versus 0 if refused.
      Under the flat 12M ceiling the worst admissible op is 12,000,000 -> 0.006795965 ETH.
      Under the sized ceiling for THIS blob it is 11,277,177 -> 0.006386608 ETH,
      removing 722,823 gas = 0.000409357 ETH of unused authority per operation.

    HOW OFTEN: at most ONCE per (account, permissionId), and only on INCLUSION.
      An operation that is never included costs nobody anything. One that IS included
      installs the id, so C4 reads true and the EntryPoint's sequence for that key
      becomes 1, so C2 fails. Both close permanently, from two independent sources.
      A second paid elevated op therefore requires a NEW permission id, i.e. a new
      signed grant POSTed by the tenant.
      The gate on the branch today bounds it at once per ADDRESS — and a fresh address
      costs one generatePrivateKey(), so that is the same bound obtained on a key that
      also excludes every honest renewal.

  paymaster fields are counted against the ceiling too (gas-limits.ts:200-208) and are
  capped at 500,000 each by PAYMASTER_GAS_MAX, so a sponsor cannot enlarge the
  admissible band by more than 1,000,000 gas = 0.000566330 ETH.
